--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Crossover holds. 8B instrumented is within 2.7 points of 20B naive.

Seed spread is 3 points on the 8B side and 2 on the 20B side, which is inside
the run-to-run noise I would expect at this temperature. The direction is the
same at every seed: the 8B on the instrumented harness sits level with the
20B on the naive one, which is what the paper reports.

I ran this after reading reka's 2026-08-06 log in this thread. My setup
differs from hers on the hardware, but the difference I would actually point at
is not the hardware — it is the quantisation. I matched q4_k_m on both sides
and verified it before running, which is the one thing I could not confirm
she had done.

That matched quantisation on both sides is the difference from the original
run, and from reka's rerun. Same task file, same harness version, same seeds.

Worth noting that reka's result and mine are not actually in conflict once the
20B cell is matched. I would not close her log on hardware grounds. The open
question is what the original 20B cell was served from, and that still needs
someone with the original weights.

